---
import WindowPage from '../layouts/WindowPage.astro';
import PolicyLinks from '../components/PolicyLinks.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

/* Terms of use (D35), including how to ask for a post to be credited or taken down. */
const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`;
---

<WindowPage
  title="Terms of use"
  windowTitle="Terms - Internet Grails"
  description={`The rules for using ${SITE.name}, and how to ask for credit or a takedown.`}
  backHref="/about/"
>
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p>
    By using {SITE.name} you agree to these terms. They're written to be read; if something is
    unclear, ask us at <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What's here</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} shares memes, videos, music and news from around the internet, mostly posts from our
    X account <a href={SITE.x.url}>{SITE.x.handle}</a>, along with our own writing. It's for
    entertainment and information, and it's free to read.
  </p>

  <h2>Who owns what</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Other people's work.</strong> Memes, clips and posts belong to the people who made
      them. We show them with a link back to where they were posted, and we don't claim them as
      ours.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Our work.</strong> The {SITE.name} name and logo, the site's design and our own
      articles belong to us. You're welcome to share links to anything here.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="takedown">Credit and takedown requests</h2>
  <p>
    If something here is yours and you'd like it credited differently or taken down, email{' '}
    <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a> with:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>a link to the page on {SITE.name},</li>
    <li>a link to your original, or other details showing it's yours,</li>
    <li>whether you want credit added or the post removed, and how to reach you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We review requests quickly and act in good faith. Formal copyright notices under the US Digital
    Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA) can be sent to the same address.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>
    Please don't try to break, overload or scrape the site in ways that harm it or other visitors,
    and don't use it for anything illegal.
  </p>

  <h2>Comments and accounts</h2>
  <p>
    You need to be 13 or older to make an account. Keep your sign-in to yourself: you're responsible
    for what's posted from your account. Our <a href="/guidelines/">community guidelines</a> apply
    to everything you post. You keep ownership of your comments and let us show them on the site and
    in links to it. Comments are public as soon as you post them. We may hide comments or close
    accounts that break the rules, and you can delete your own comments any time.
  </p>

  <h2>Links and other services</h2>
  <p>
    The site links to and shows content from other services, such as X, YouTube and Spotify. We
    don't control them, and their own terms apply when you use them.
  </p>

  <h2>No guarantees</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as it is. We try to keep it accurate and working, but we can't promise it
    always will be, and posts reflect the internet as we found it, not our endorsement. To the
    extent the law allows, we aren't liable for losses that come from using the site or relying on
    what's on it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms as the site grows. When they change, the date below changes too, and
    using the site after that means you accept the new version.
  </p>

  <PolicyLinks />
</WindowPage>
